# NEG (Round XXV Track B — one-sided-combinator class): Option.map_err does
# NOT exist in the phase-0 subset. Ratified Result-only per
# `docs/language-reference.md:3861-3891` (Option has one payload; there is
# no Error axis for `.map_err` to apply to).
#
# Pre-fix (RED-verified 2026-08-02): Rust `gg check` prints "OK: no semantic
# errors" then `gg build` crashes at C-compile with
# `'__gg_Option__int64_t' has no member named 'None_0'; did you mean
# 'Some_0'?` (the lowerer materialises a bogus `None_0` axis for map_err
# on Option); ggdef `run` REJECTED at eval-time with `IllFormed`
# "`.map_err()` on Option is outside the phase-0 subset (Result-only)"
# (eval.rs:1731-1733) — too late for corpus_b `CheckFails` adjudication.
# Core #8 both-wrong class.
#
# Post-fix: ggdef `elaborate_method` REJECTS at elaborate-time with
# `error[E_NoMethodFound]: `.map_err()` on Option is outside the phase-0
# subset (Result-only)` (XXV Track B). Rust `typecheck` REJECTS with
# `error[E_NoMethodFound]: no method `map_err` found on type `Option[int]
# — `.map_err()` is outside the phase-0 subset (Result-only)`` via the
# `reject_wrong_receiver_combinator` chokepoint (Round XXVI Track A).

void main():
    Option[int] o = Some(5)
    Option[int] o2 = o.map_err((int x): x + 1)
    print(0)
